conductor-files for Debian and Ubuntu
=====================================

conductor-files runs on a Samba domain-member file server, never on a
domain controller. The package installs the agent, its unit and the
conffile /etc/conductor-files/agent.toml (root 0644, roots = /srv/shares).
It does not enable or start anything.

  1. Join the server to the domain with "include = registry" and
     "vfs objects = acl_xattr" (docs/install.md, section 1).
  2. Create the share roots (root-owned, not writable by others) and list
     them in agent.toml and in a drop-in, since the unit's file system is
     read-only elsewhere:
       sudo install -d /etc/systemd/system/conductor-files.service.d
       printf '[Service]\nReadWritePaths=/srv/shares\n' | \
         sudo tee /etc/systemd/system/conductor-files.service.d/roots.conf
  3. sudo systemctl daemon-reload
     sudo systemctl enable --now conductor-files
     sudo conductor-files check
  4. sudo conductor-files enroll-code, then add the server in conductor.

Upgrades restart the agent when it is running. "apt purge conductor-files"
deletes /etc/conductor-files, /var/lib/conductor-files (key pair, pinned
conductor keys, audit log) and the roots.conf drop-in; shares and folders
are left as they are.

Full guide: https://github.com/openbasalt/samba-conductor-files/blob/main/docs/install.md
